  "configuration_id": "config_026",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_010 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat; acc 0.6287), which showed a large jump over singleprofile (~0.535) and outperformed transformer aggregation (0.599). However, in the multiprofile setting we have only tested concat fusion. In singleprofile, concat vs weighted was nearly identical (0.535 vs 0.532), but the multiprofile+avgpool pipeline produces richer, higher-dimensional representations where the fusion mechanism may interact differently. Question: config_026 (identical to config_010 but with weighted fusion) isolates the effect of fusion strategy in the multiprofile+avgpool regime. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a clean single-variable comparison against our current best, directly tests whether the fusion choice matters at the new performance level, and the answer will inform whether further multiprofile experiments should use concat or weighted. This is more informative than changing the image encoder (image alone was very weak at 0.23, so its contribution is likely secondary) or the RNA encoder (pca_n2000 already showed clear advantage over scgpt), and it avoids confounding multiple design choices simultaneously."
}

